  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math> <mi>z</mi> </math> be positive real numbers. Suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math> <mi>z</mi> </math> are the lengths of the sides of a triangle opposite to its angles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> and <math> <mi>Z</mi> </math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;then which of the following statements is/are TRUE?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2nfgd",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
